"In that prison, we have to arrange for him to learn how to grow vegetables and provide vocational training for him. Set up a place to grow a lot of vegetables to sell and set up a training place such as weaving, carving and cooking.
Speaking at a meeting on the dissemination of the Royal Decree on mitigation of pardons and the strengthening of work requesting amnesty on February 17, 2021, Mr. Keut Rith stated that prisons are a place for educating people to change and stop committing crimes. Further offenses.
But at the same time, there needs to be vocational training for them because Cambodia does not have the death penalty law.
"The prison is a place to arrange vocational training for him to have a job, and this is where I will talk more with the professional officials of the Ministry of Interior."
Nuth Savana, spokesman for the General Department of Prisons of the Ministry of Interior, also said that vocational training programs for inmates are available in all prisons in Cambodia, but it depends on the size of the prison.
Separately, for Trapeang Phlong Prison in Tbong Khmum Province, the rehabilitation program includes handicrafts, pure water production, wood and metal furniture processing, and technical skills in vegetable cultivation, prevention and animal husbandry.
Mr. Savana confirmed that:
"As a strategic plan, we need to make these programs available in all prisons, depending on the size of each prison location."
Mr. Soeung Senkaruna, Senior Human Rights Monitor of the Association (ADHOC), welcomed the initiative to provide vocational training to inmates.
He urged to start discussing this plan as soon as possible and seek help from relevant institutions to implement as soon as possible so that the prisoners or convicts have the professional skills to be able to work when they return.
